{"name":"Lighter Mint","hex":"#dfebdd","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"lighter","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A person who lights (“sets fire to or ignites”) a thing.","An electrical or mechanical device, usually handheld and reusable, used to light things; especially, a device which creates a small flame to light cigarettes, stoves, etc."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A boat, usually a flat-bottomed barge, for carrying loads across short distances, especially one for loading and unloading a larger ship, and to transport cargo between such a ship and a wharf."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lighter"},{"term":"mint","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A building or institution where money (originally, only coins) is produced under government licence.","A vast sum of money;  a large amount of something."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To reproduce (coins), usually en masse, under licence.","To invent; to forge; to fabricate; to fashion."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mint"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lighter","blocks":[{"text":"A lighter is a portable device which uses mechanical or electrical means to create a controlled flame, and can be used to ignite a variety of flammable items, such as cigarettes, butane gas, fireworks, candles, or campfires. Some lighters use a consumable chemical fuel, others use electricity from a battery."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c9/White_lighter_with_flame.JPG/330px-White_lighter_with_flame.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lighter","wikidata":"Q20459"},{"title":"Spring green","blocks":[{"text":"Spring green is a color that was traditionally considered to be on the yellow side of green, but in modern computer systems based on the RGB color model is halfway between cyan and green on the color wheel."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org